# R23 The Goat's Stand (side quest, comic). By hand, polished by Gemini, unvoiced.

~ board
Narrator: A notice, on a board, over which stands a goat. The goat has chosen to stand on the board. The notice says the board is the evacuation point.
the_notice_goat [neutral]: The goat chews, and holds your eye with a look of absolute disinterest.
set wv_goat_met
quest the_goats_stand asked
-> menu

~ menu
* [Animal Handling DC 13] Coax the goat down -> moved | bitten
* [Intimidation DC 14] Stare the goat down -> moved | bitten
* [if item:wv_feast_bread] Offer the goat a heel of the last loaf -> bread
* Ask Tamsin to move the evacuation point instead -> point
* [ends:the_goats_stand] Leave the goat where it is -> stand
* Leave -> END

~ bitten
Narrator: The goat reaches out, takes your sleeve in its mouth, and pulls, and holds your eye the whole time.
damage 1d4 piercing
-> menu

~ moved
Narrator: Some silent treaty passes between you. The goat steps off the board with the dignity of a magistrate leaving a bad court, and walks toward the church without looking back.
quest the_goats_stand moved
set goat_resolved
set goat_saved
-> END

~ bread
Narrator: The goat takes the bread. The goat considers the bread. The goat gets down off the board with exactly the speed of a creature that was always going to do it, and was only waiting for a better offer.
take wv_feast_bread
quest the_goats_stand moved
set goat_resolved
set goat_saved
-> END

~ point
Narrator: Tamsin has the evacuation notice moved to the well in forty seconds and a stamp. The goat is on the board, and the board is not the point, and the goat, as far as anyone can tell, is satisfied.
quest the_goats_stand moved
set goat_resolved
set goat_saved
-> END

~ stand
Narrator: The goat looks at you the way it looked at the sky, and goes on chewing. Whatever walks down the hill tonight is going to meet that expression.
quest the_goats_stand stands
set goat_resolved
set goat_stood
-> END
